cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the thesis below."
title: "Comparison of graph-based algorithmic strategies for controlling the spread of misinformation"
abstract: >-
  Code accompanying a bachelor thesis comparing graph-based node-immunization
  strategies (random, degree, betweenness centrality, community bridge) for
  containing misinformation spread, modeled as a stochastic SIR process on the
  SNAP Facebook and Twitter ego networks, with a community-level fairness
  analysis using the Gini coefficient.
type: software
